assertion  XSH.iswalpha.001
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswalpha() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class alpha as the locale definition lists it: the 26
           uppercase and the 26 lowercase letters.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswalpha.002
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswalpha() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the ten digits, the 32 punctuation characters, the six
           white-space characters, and the control characters.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswalpha.003
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswalpha(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswalpha.004
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each of the 128 characters, iswalpha() is non-zero exactly when
           iswupper() or iswlower() is non-zero.
test       t/004-alpha-is-upper-or-lower.c

assertion  XSH.iswalpha.005
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalpha.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale, iswalpha() is still non-zero for the 52 letters.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
